-- title:
--   Supersingular places enumerate the crossings, with width and j-pin
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $5 \le p$ and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, a package $\mathfrak X$ of type `DRModelPackage p` for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the full modular function field of level $p$, an algebraically closed perfect field $k$ of characteristic $p$, a ring map $red : A \to k$, modular polynomial data for $p$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, integrality of the two Hecke degeneracy maps $\bar\alpha,\bar\beta$ at level $1$, and a specialisation datum $P$ of type `PlaceSpecialization`. Let $W$ be a finset of places of `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces p 1 k`, and let $e$ be a function with $e(w) =$ `jWidth` of $w$'s evaluation of the generator `jGeomGen k 1` for $w \in W$, that is $3$, $2$ or $1$ according as that $j$-value is $0$, $1728$ or neither. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal generated by $p$, together with a ring isomorphism $e_O$ of $O$ onto the contraction of $A$ to the fixed field of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$, a fraction field $K$ of $O$, an embedding $\iota_K : K \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ compatible with $e_O$ and mapping $O$ into $A$, and $to\kappa : O \to k$ the composite of $\iota_K$ with $red$. Let $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ be a `DRResolvedModelPackage` for $\mathfrak X$ over $O$ with residue field $k$ via $to\kappa$, let the base change of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\mathbb Z \to O$ be integral, and let $\varphi$ be a ring embedding of the function field of that base change into `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` which is pinned on constants (it sends the germ of $a \in O$ to $\iota_K(a)$) and on the finite chart (it sends each element of the chart algebra `chartAlgFin` to its $q$-expansion via `coeffEmb`), the relevant finite-chart open being nonempty. Assume further that each node $n$ of $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ admits $\hat\jmath \in O$ and an element $t$ of the maximal ideal of the stalk at the image of `nodeEquiv n` under `pullback.fst (𝔛.compInf k) (𝔛.compZero k)` followed by `𝔛.compInf k` followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`, with $\varphi(t) =$ `jFun 1 p` $- \iota_K(\hat\jmath)$, and that whenever such $\hat\jmath, t$ exist for a node $n$ one has `𝔛reg.width n` $=$ `jWidth` of $red(\iota_K(\hat\jmath))$. The conclusion is the existence of a bijection $\sigma_N$ from $W$ onto the nodes of $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ such that the width of $\sigma_N(w)$ equals $e(w)$ for all $w \in W$, and such that for every $w \in W$ there are $\hat\jmath \in O$ with $red(\iota_K(\hat\jmath))$ equal to $w$'s evaluation of `jGeomGen k 1` and an element $t$ of the maximal ideal of the stalk at the image point attached to $\sigma_N(w)$ as above with $\varphi(t) =$ `jFun 1 p` $- \iota_K(\hat\jmath)$.
--
--   This is the enumeration of the crossings of the two components of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$ by the supersingular $j$-invariants in characteristic $p$, together with the thickness law $1,2,3$ governed by $j = 0, 1728$ and the pinning of each crossing by the local equation $j - \hat\jmath$. It feeds the dictionary identifying the components and their intersection data in [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_nodeEquiv_swap_forall_comp_eq_dict_of_sections_of_charts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_nodeEquiv_swap_forall_comp_eq_dict_of_sections_of_charts).
